{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1560,1590p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '570,610p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc; sed -n '1,45p' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn error|first-pending|update-at' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc | head -15; sed -n '1920,1938p' test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc; rg -n 'link-refused' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- link-read-step\n  \"Apply one read outcome `r` to the `:link-response` `entry`, whose\n   `:cursor` is the position the read was made at (section 7.2, step 7):\n   an `ok` carrying another id's response advances the cursor and skips\n   it, `[:skipped state entry]`; every other result is final,\n   `[:done state waiting woken]`. An `ok` with the entry's own id settles;\n   `blocked` keeps waiting; `gap` and the terminal outcomes are raised as\n   the effect's error.\"\n  [state entry r]\n  (let [o (outcome r)]\n    (case o\n      :dao.stream/ok\n      (let [v (:dao.stream/value r)\n            id (when (map? v) (:yin.link/id v))\n            entry (assoc entry :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))]\n        (if (= id (:link-id entry))\n          (into [:done] (settle state entry v))\n          [:skipped (skip state entry id) entry]))\n      :dao.stream/blocked [:done state entry nil]\n      [:done\n       (retire state (:link-id entry) :restored)\n       nil\n       (refused-entry entry\n                      {:status :refused,\n                       :reason :link-stream,\n                       :outcome o,\n                       :link-id (:link-id entry)})])))\n\n\n(defn- poll-link-response\n  \"Poll a `:link-response` entry's kept cursor (section 7.2, step 7):\n   and the append are the driver's: the entry is built without `:cursor`\n   and parks in `:link-request` with nothing sent. The entry is the kernel's\n   registers plus the link fields: resource ids and plain data, never a\n   handle.\n\n   A module already on this task's install ancestry is `:require-cycle`\n   naming the chain (section 7.4): the child that asked is refused. A VM\n   composed without a link pair cannot link, so its miss fails as v1's\n   did, naming the modules it has.\"\n  [state effect {:keys [park-entry-fns]} try?]\n  (let [module-name (:module effect)\n        build (or (when try? (get park-entry-fns :module/try-require))\n                  (get park-entry-fns :module/require))\n        registers #(cond-> (if build (build state effect nil) {})\n                     try? (assoc :try? true))\n        resources (:resources state)\n        response (get resources link-response-resource)]\n    (cond\n      (some? (resolve-module (:modules state) module-name))\n      {:value (if try? {:status :ok, :module module-name} module-name),\n       :state state, :blocked? false}\n\n      (some #{module-name} (:ancestry state))\n      (let [refusal {:reason :require-cycle,\n                     :module module-name,\n                     :chain (conj (vec (:ancestry state)) module-name)}]\n        (if try?\n          {:value (assoc refusal :status :refused),\n           :state state, :blocked? false}\n          (throw (ex-info \"Require cycle\" refusal))))\n\n      (installing? state module-name)\n      (block-on state (cond-> (assoc (registers)\n                                     :reason :install :name module-name)\n                        try? (assoc :link-id (get-in state\n                                                     [:installs module-name\n                                                      :parent]))))\n\n      (not (and response (get resources link-request-resource)))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Module is not in this VM's registry\"\n                      {:module module-name,\n(ns yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.ledger :as ledger]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]))\n193:(defn error\n608:(defn first-pending\n621:      (is (= (:reason world) (first (:slots (first-pending task)))) \"law 3: the observed wait's reason\"))\n745:        (is (= [:install 'host.mod false] (:slots (first-pending (root-task wire)))))\n825:(defn update-at\n830:      (update-in x [:slots (first path)] update-at (rest path) f)\n831:      (update x (first path) update-at (rest path) f))))\n905:      (fn [task] (update-at task (conj wait-act 3) #(rebuild % (fn [ps] (conj ps [(free-register task (act-of task)) [:lit :x]])))))]\n907:      (fn [task] (update-at task (conj wait-act 3) #(rebuild % (fn [ps] (vec (rest ps))))))]\n910:        (update-at task (conj wait-act 3)\n913:      (fn [task] (update-at task (conj wait-act 5) inc))]\n915:      (fn [task] (update-at task [13 0 1] (constantly (rows/node :pending [:install 'bogus false]))))]\n917:      (fn [task] (update-at task (conj wait-act 3) #(rebuild % (fn [ps] (vec (remove (fn [[_ v]] (= [:lit nil] v)) ps))))))]\n923:      (fn [task] (update-at task [8] (constantly (rows/node :parked-table [:bogus (act-of task)]))))]\n925:      (fn [task] (update-at task [5] #(rebuild % (fn [ps] (conj ps ['yin/def [:lit 1]])))))]]))\n\n(deftest trusted-fallback-names-its-trust\n  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n        {:keys [H R h-index]} (mint-root store worked-example)\n        pairing (linker/pairing-datoms 'root H R)\n        res (linker/trusted-fallback (h-runtime store h-index) 'root pairing\n                                     receiver)]\n    (is (linker/ok? res))\n    (is (= :composition (:trust res)))\n    (is (= {:root 'root, :from R} (:fallback res)))\n    (is (= H (:identity res)))\n    (is (= :yin.debruijn.code (:format res)))\n    (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :absent, :root 'elsewhere}\n           (linker/trusted-fallback (h-runtime store h-index) 'elsewhere\n                                    pairing receiver)))\n    (jing/close! store)))\n\n\n(deftest verifying-fallback-re-lowers-the-named-root\n1165:    (assoc (ready entry nil) :status :link-refused :refusal refusal)))\n2248:      (= :link-refused status) status\n2264:    (= :link-refused o)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1735,1765p;2257,2275p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '195,202p' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn.*loss|defn.*refus|defn.*abandon' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '1,60p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1735,1765p;2257,2275p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '195,202p' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; rg -n 'defn.*loss|defn.*refus|defn.*abandon' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '1,60p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"                                 {:status :lost,\n                                  :reason reason,\n                                  :link-id link-id})))\n      state)))\n\n\n(defn abandon-installs\n  \"A composition gives up on every install in flight (the abandoned case\n   of section 7.2, step 7, reaching section 7.3's `refused`): each child\n   is dropped -- nothing from its store is published -- and every\n   `:install` waiter receives loss data for try-require or an effect error\n   for require. The install entry is removed; a later require may retry. A\n   state with no installs is unchanged. The dropped children's own link\n   ids are never minted again by a state that carries `:origins` forward\n   past them.\"\n  [state reason]\n  (reduce (fn [state module-name]\n            (refuse-install state module-name\n                            {:status :lost, :reason reason}))\n          state\n          (keys (:installs state))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; FFI response routing\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Several callers may read one call-out, and one VM may wait on several\n;; response cells (its own call-out cursor, and the carried cells of\n;; lowered retained calls). The generic sweep delivers positionally -- a\n;; woken reader takes whatever value its cell holds next -- and\n   waitset diagnostic names its status and the entry that earned it: there\n   is no stream operation whose error vocabulary it belongs to.\"\n  [entry o]\n  (cond\n    (contains? waitset-diagnostics o)\n    (fail \"Wait-set entry woke with a diagnostic\" {:status o, :entry entry})\n    ;; a refused or lost link, or a refused install: the effect's error\n    (= :link-refused o)\n    (fail (str \"Module link refused: \"\n               (clojure.core/name (or (:reason (:refusal entry)) :refused)))\n          (assoc (:refusal entry) :link-module (:name entry)))\n    ;; an FFI response stream that can no longer answer this call\n    (contains? ffi/response-loss-statuses o)\n    (ffi/throw-response-lost! (ffi/response-call-id entry) o)\n    (= :next (:reason entry))\n    (fail \"Stream read failed\"\n          {:outcome o,\n           :stream-id (:stream-id entry),\n           :cursor-id (:id (:cursor-ref entry))})\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn cat-of\n413:(defn- wake-refusal?\n484:(defn- gate-refuse!\n703:(defn- refuse-unminted!\n1156:(defn- refused-entry\n1254:(defn- error-refusal\n1344:(defn- refuse-install\n1719:(defn abandon-link\n1741:(defn abandon-installs\n---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \"Remote test servers\" below for\n# which lanes may overlap.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat >> test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc <<'EOF'\n\n\n(defn try-wrapper\n  [try?]\n  (if try? #(s/let1 'require (s/v 'try-require) %) identity))\n\n\n(deftest link-refusal-keeps-each-return-contract-after-handoff\n  (doseq [try? [true false] tail? [false true] retained? [false true]]\n    (testing (pr-str {:try? try? :tail? tail? :retained? retained?})\n      (let [world (linking (try-wrapper try?) tail? retained?)\n            m (:machine world)\n            entry (first (:wait-set m))\n            response (get (:resources m) module/link-response-resource)\n            refusal {:yin.link/id (:link-id entry) :status :refused :reason :absent}\n            answer\"'! #(stream/append! response refusal)\n            world (assoc world :steps (if retained? [(first (:steps world)) answer!] [answer!]))]\n        (is (= try? (boolean (:try? entry))) \"the source waiter has the requested contract\")\n        (if try?\n          (let [{:keys [halted value recv wire]} (handed-off world)]\n            (is halted)\n            (is (= (assoc refusal :module '\"'host.mod) value))\n            (is (true? (:try? (first (:wait-set recv)))))\n            (is (= wire (rows/emit (rows/decode wire))) \\\"pack round trip includes the flag\\\"))\n          (let [failure (error #(handed-off world))]\n            (is (= :absent (:reason failure)))\n            (is (= 'host.mod (:link-module failure)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest install-return-contract-and-link-flag-validation\n  (doseq [try? [true false]]\n    (let [world (installing (try-wrapper try?) false nil)\n          {:keys [toy serve\"'!]} (served #{:reader :writer})\n          wire (rows/lift-task (:machine world) serve! (lift-opts))\n          pending (first-pending (root-task wire))\n          attach! (s/remote-attacher toy)\n          recv (rows/lower-task (machine) wire attach!)\n          abandoned (engine/abandon-install